    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `locality`, a read-only derived field on `Owner` that maps a city to its canonical region.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`LocalityResolver.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility unit holding the fixed city-to-region table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and one static `regionFor(city)` method returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`. This keeps the lookup table out of the entity so `Owner` doesn't become a catch-all.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getLocality()` getter that delegates to `LocalityResolver.regionFor(city)`, following the exact pattern of the other derived getters (`getMembershipTier`, `getDisplayName`, `getInitials`).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `locality` read-only property to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and MapStruct auto-maps it from the getter (same mechanism used for `membershipTier`).\n\nNo new copying: the derived-field/DTO plumbing reuses the existing `@Transient`-getter + MapStruct auto-mapping convention already in place.",
